<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  Template for the CINE drone as the real airframe in Gazebo: a TBS Source One 5-inch
  frame, four EMAX ECO II 2207 1700KV motors, Gemfan 51366 props, a 6S battery and the Pi
  stack, with the same fixed Pi camera as cine_iris. The ArduPilot plugin, rotor joint
  order and LiftDrag layout follow ardupilot_gazebo's iris_with_ardupilot (commit
  f116b03552d05c8d0b0bed5ed67033a1183121d1; see models/ATTRIBUTION.md); the geometry,
  mass and thrust numbers are the real vehicle's. gazebo_sim.launch.py fills {{camera}} and
  {{imu_axes_noise}} through cine_gazebo.model_rendering; never load this file directly.

  Mass blocks (box inertias; metres, kilograms; block sizes are assumed, the masses are
  weighed). base_link carries all of them, its inertial computed by
  model_rendering.composite_inertia (a test checks the totals):
    4 motors with props   0.036 each, 0.03 x 0.03 x 0.03 at (+-0.07265, +-0.0865, 0)
    frame                 0.300, 0.14 x 0.10 x 0.03 at the origin
    battery               0.213, 0.075 x 0.035 x 0.047 at z -0.026
    Pi stack              0.100, 0.065 x 0.056 x 0.03 at z +0.041
  Total 0.757 kg (1.67 lb weighed with battery), centre of gravity z -0.0019 m.
  The rotor links add 4 x 0.001 kg so each can spin as its own link, and the camera link
  0.0001 kg (the Pi stack's weighed mass already includes the camera).

  Thrust: each prop is three LiftDrag blades 120 degrees apart at r = 0.0486 m. With cla
  4.25, a0 0.3 and blade area 2.308e-4 m^2 the thrust coefficient is k = 1.2552e-6
  N/(rad/s)^2; the ArduPilot plugin's multiplier 3666 rad/s at full command follows from
  it.

  Rotor spin: ArduPilot's quad-X numbering, motor 1 front-right CCW, 2 back-left CCW, 3
  front-left CW, 4 back-right CW, on channels 0 to 3; the model's +x is forward and +y is
  left.

  Looks: the visuals are meshes in meshes/, written in metres in base_link's frame except
  the props, which are centred on their rotor links. Each has its colours in the .mtl
  beside it except the carbon (twill texture) and the clear props (translucent material
  below). The geometry is the TBS Source One V5 CAD, the
  Raspberry Pi 5 and Camera Module 3 CAD, the owner's printed parts and a few generated
  pieces (wiring, standoffs). The motors, stack, props and guards come from CAD that may not
  be redistributed, so their meshes (restricted_*) stay out of git and those visuals are
  missing on a fresh checkout; see models/ATTRIBUTION.md. Visuals only: collision and
  inertia above still use the mass blocks.

  Rotor joint control: p_gain is the Iris's 0.20 scaled by the rotor inertia (6e-6 here
  against the Iris's 1.7e-4) so P * dt / I stays near the Iris's value at the 1 ms step.
  Not yet run in Gazebo.
-->
